"The blight spreads from the Hollow, an old sealed dungeon under the Mother Beech in the deep wood."
"A Night Order mage is feeding blightstones to the Hollow's core to turn it into a blight dungeon."
"She lives as a charcoal-burner called Mother Sallow in the smoking hut by the Wren Brook."
"The corrupted beasts are the Hollow's overflow, pushed out as its core sours."
"If nothing stops her, the Hollow wakes as a blight dungeon at the thaw's end, about thirty days on."
"A woken blight dungeon would pour corrupted beasts over the Wrenmark, Merrowgate first."
"Old Greyhand the treant has rooted itself across the Hollow's mouth to hold the blight in."
"Old Greyhand is weakening, and its bark is blackening from the roots up."
"Cal Fenn saw Mother Sallow at work; she took him, and he is alive in the Hollow, half-corrupted."
